    "journey.phase.schedule.desc": "Sequence the work in time, link cost to schedule (5D), and plan crews, equipment and risk.",
    "glossary.retention_example": "On a 100,000 invoice with 5% retainage, 5,000 is withheld and released at handover.",
    "glossary.nrm": "The UK measurement and cost-classification rules for estimates and bid schedules (New Rules of Measurement).",
    "glossary.gaeb": "The German electronic exchange format for tenders and bid schedules, used to send and receive priced work items.",
    "glossary.masterformat": "The North American standard that organizes construction work into numbered divisions and sections.",
    "glossary.snag_example": "A scratched door noted at inspection is a punch item to fix before sign-off.",
    "about.ai_desc": "OpenConstructionERP includes optional AI-powered tools, quick estimation from text descriptions, smart cost suggestions, and bid schedule chat assistant. These features require an API key from a provider of your choice (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google). AI is always opt-in: it only activates when you configure it, and you decide what data to send. Without an API key, all other features work fully offline.",
    "agents.builder.role_placeholder": "a senior cost estimator",
    "agents.builder.delete_message": "This removes the agent from your catalog. Past runs are kept. This cannot be undone.",
    "agents.triggers.schedule_variance_recorded.description": "Fire the agent when a schedule variance is logged (e.g. draft a delay note).",
    "about.cap.boq": "Bid Schedule",
    "about.cap.boq_desc": "Create detailed bid schedule with hierarchical sections, positions, assemblies, markups (overhead, profit, VAT), and automatic totals. Supports DIN 276, NRM 1/2, MasterFormat, and custom classification systems.",
    "about.cap.catalog_desc": "7,000+ resources, materials, equipment, labor, operators, and utilities. Build reusable assemblies (composite rates) from catalog items and apply them directly to bid schedule positions.",
    "about.cap.schedule_desc": "Create project schedules with CPM critical path calculation, interactive Gantt charts, Monte Carlo risk analysis, resource assignment, and auto-generation of activities from your bid schedule.",
    "about.intro": "OpenConstructionERP is a modern platform for construction cost management. It covers the full estimation workflow, from creating a bid schedule to tendering and bid comparison. Designed for professionals worldwide, it supports international standards and works in 20 languages.",
    "about.intro_body": "Shows your installed version, recent release notes, the AGPL-3.0 license and the open-source story behind the platform, plus links to the wider DataDrivenConstruction ecosystem and the cost-estimation book. Use it to confirm what build you are on before reporting an issue or planning an upgrade.",
    "about.intro_more": "About is where you confirm what build you are running and learn the story behind it. The top of the page shows your installed version, an open-source badge, the AGPL-3.0 license chip and a list of the most recent releases, with an update notification when a newer version is available. Scroll down for the platform capability stats, the founder's note on why the project exists, the full AGPL-3.0 license broken into plain \"you can\" and \"you must\" lists, documentation links, the changelog, and ways to support the project. It is a read-only information page, nothing here changes your data.\n\nIt links out to the wider ecosystem rather than into your project records:\n\n- Jump to **Modules** to see what is installed, or **Settings** to configure the workspace.\n- The page links to the DataDrivenConstruction ecosystem, the open-source repositories and the free Data-Driven Construction book.\n\n**Getting the most out of it:**\n\n- Check the version number here before reporting an issue or planning an upgrade.\n- The recent-releases list and changelog show the cadence, so you can see what changed between your build and the latest.\n- The license \"you can / you must\" lists spell out the AGPL trade-off in plain terms before you self-host or fork.",
