    "settings.remove_demo_desc": "Permanently delete the sample projects and everything inside them (bid schedules, documents, schedules). Your own projects and all user accounts are kept, and the sample content will not come back on restart.",
    "submittals.intro_body": "Log each shop drawing, product data sheet, sample or certificate and move it through Draft, Submitted, Under Review, then Approved or Revise-and-resubmit, with a due-date and days-in-court badge so nothing stalls. Link a submittal to the bid schedule positions it covers so you can see which items have approved documentation before they go to site.",
    "submittals.intro_more": "Press **New Submittal**, give it a title and spec section, pick the type (shop drawing, product data, sample, mock-up, test report, certificate or warranty) and a date required. The submittal starts as Draft, then you Submit it for review. A reviewer opens it and records a decision: Approved, Approved as Noted, Revise and Resubmit, or Rejected, with comments. A Revise-and-resubmit sends it back so the submitter edits and resubmits as the next revision.\n\nThe row carries a days-in-court badge and a due-date countdown so nothing stalls. Where your project has a submittal approval route configured under Governance, a multi-step sign-off runs instead of the direct review. Submittals can link to the bid schedule positions they cover, and supporting files live in Documents.\n\n**Getting the most out of it:**\n- Link each submittal to its bid schedule positions so you can see what has approved documentation before it goes to site.\n- Watch the days-in-court badge to chase a slow reviewer.",
