    "cases.classify_the_delivery_route_for_a_work_package.step.confirm.what": "Walk the classified route past whoever owns schedule and design sign-off, and lock it in as the route the package will actually follow.",
    "cases.register_source_data_before_it_blocks_the_schedule.desc": "Register the source documents the project depends on, verify them, see what is expiring or missing against the schedule, and clear the blockers before they stop work.",
    "cases.register_source_data_before_it_blocks_the_schedule.step.check-schedule.title": "See what is expiring or missing against the schedule",
    "cases.register_source_data_before_it_blocks_the_schedule.step.check-schedule.why": "The cost of a missing document is not the document, it is the crew standing idle on the day the activity was due to start. Checking against the schedule is what turns a filing gap into a schedule risk you can actually see.",
    "cases.run_a_site_supervision_visit.step.plan-visit.why": "A visit with no plan turns into whatever is visible on the day, and hidden works that needed checking get covered before anyone thought to look. Planning against the schedule is what catches the point before it is missed.",
    "cases.run_a_site_supervision_visit.step.plan-visit.in.programme": "Schedule of works",
    "cases.run_a_site_supervision_visit.step.compare.what": "Set what was actually observed against what the drawings and the schedule said should be there, and pull out anywhere the two disagree.",
    "cases.run_an_authority_design_review_cycle.step.open-cycle.why": "An open cycle with a deadline is what stops a review sitting unanswered until it becomes a schedule problem. Everyone can see it is live and whose turn it is to act.",
    "cases.submit_a_permit_package_to_the_authority.step.submit.why": "A submission that only lives in someone's inbox is a submission the rest of the team cannot plan around. Tracking it against the record keeps the schedule honest about when approval will actually land.",
